Z||000015||Notchit||02-02-2001||01:45 AM||||BAH!<BR>i bought a Dreamcast last year and sold it this summer, thank god.<BR>Sega has always screwed their customers EX- 32x, Sega CD, Sega Gamegear, Sega Nomad, Sega Pico, Sega Saturn AND now, newly added to the long list, Sega Dreamcast.<BR>I will never buy another new sega product again.<BR>I have a master system and I love it, i look for games at garage sales ect.<BR>The older games were the funnest, like Nintendo games (NES) <BR>Now, i stick to PC games, better graphics, sound, ect. I bought a PSX controller for the PC, man i think its great. Right now i have Tony Hawk 2 on my computer, fun game!<P>X-box is just a way for microsoft to make even more money, god knows they need it.<BR>I am unsure if it will flourish like the Playstation did. Nintentos Cube system doen't look too promising either...<P>just my 2 cents  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Seein Red<BR>'85 Fiero GT<BR>ICQ#: 56708070<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Outside_side2(sml2).jpg"> <BR>_________________________||||reg||4
Z||000016||DJRice||02-02-2001||09:32 AM||||I have an N64, and it will probably be the last game system I buy (for me,anyway).  Game systems basically PCs without keyboards anymore.  Why in the world anyone would by one for $300 or more vs $400-$500 for an inexpensive PC nowadays is beyond me.  <P>Dreamcast was powered by Windows CE.  X-box will no doubt be powered by some sort of Windows environment.  PS2 plays DVDs.  N64 was going to have a floppy drive.  The game systems are basically becoming PCs that are not as funtional as a normal desktop.  <P>I have a PII 450 with 256MB ram and a 16MB 3D card.  Although I havent purchased any new games over the past year or so, all of the games I have played basically blew away anything that N64 or PS or Dreamcast could do as far as graphics, speed, and control. (NFS Hot Pursuit, Viper Racing, Starcraft)  Now you have steering wheels and game controllers that emulate what comes with the game systems so I dont see the point of a system for strickly gaming any more.  <P>But Microsoft will sell the living hell out of those X-boxes that will play games and surf the net.  People will buy expansion keyboards and other stuff.  And they will end up with an almost fully funtional PC in the end that they have spent $1000 on.  When they could have bought a sub $1000 PC that was more capable and has an infinitely better variety of games.  <P>Boy did that ever turn into a soapbox speech.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
